                  "title": "Paid Time Off Policy",
                  "section": "3.2",
                  "section_heading": "Company holidays inside PTO",
                  "text": "A company holiday that falls inside your PTO dates is not deducted from your PTO balance. Only your scheduled working days are charged. Which days are company holidays depends on your home office calendar; see the Holiday Calendar & Observance policy (RSE-HOL-01 \u00a71.3).\nWhen you enter dates in the HR Portal, it works out the PTO days for you using your home office's calendar. For example, for an employee of a US office, a request for Wednesday to Friday in a week where Wednesday is a US company holiday is charged as 2 PTO days. The same request from an employee of the Toronto office may be charged differently, because the Toronto office follows the Canada calendar.",
